#: src/PageHelp.php:37
msgid ""
"The information security management system dashboard: risks, controls, "
"incidents, deadlines and reviews at a glance."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:42
msgid ""
"Click a card to open the matching list. The dashboard menu lets you add or "
"move cards, and share it with other profiles."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:49
msgid ""
"The cyber maturity score (0 to 100): an overview of the progress of your "
"security management system, computed from your data."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:54
msgid ""
"Present it in management reviews; the calculation details show which "
"components to improve first."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:62
msgid ""
"Before an audit, this page gathers the inconsistencies of your security "
"management system: risks without an owner, controls without evidence, "
"expired evidence, policies not reviewed, nonconformities closed without "
"action, and more."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:68
msgid ""
"Start with the high severity gaps. Click an item to open it, fix it, then "
"come back: the page is computed again each time. Nothing is changed "
"automatically. Export the list (CSV or PDF) to follow the preparation of the "
"audit."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:77
msgid ""
"At each surveillance audit, the certification body checks that the findings "
"of its previous audit have been dealt with. This page lists those findings "
"(nonconformities, areas of concern, opportunities for improvement) with "
"their corrective action, their evidence and whether they are lifted."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:84
msgid ""
"Record each certification audit with its type, then its findings in the "
"Findings tab of the audit, with the reference given by the body. Treat each "
"finding (cause, action, owner, due date, evidence in the Documents tab) "
"until it is verified. Export the PDF and hand it to the auditor at the "
"opening meeting of the next audit."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:94
msgid ""
"This page guides you, step by step, from setting up your security management "
"system to the certification audit: for each step, it shows what is expected, "
"where you stand according to the data already entered, and the screen to "
"open to complete it."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:100
msgid ""
"Follow the steps in order, starting with the one marked as the next step. "
"Click its button to open the screen concerned, complete it, then come back: "
"the page is computed again each time. Nothing is changed automatically. Give "
"the target date of the audit (or plan the certification audit): each step "
"not done gets an advised deadline, shown in the compliance calendar, and the "
"owner is warned when one risks being late. Export the PDF readiness report "
"to share where you stand."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:111
msgid ""
"Everything waiting for you in the security management system, on one page "
"and sorted by due date."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:115
msgid ""
"Start with the overdue items highlighted in red, then open each line to act "
"on it. The number next to the menu entry counts these items."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:123
msgid ""
"The documents an audit is waiting for from you: each request says what is "
"expected, for which control and by when."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:128
msgid ""
"Add the files (or an existing evidence of the control) to each request, then "
"submit it to the audit. If the audit asks you to complete a request, its "
"reason is shown in red."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:132
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, clause 9.2 (internal audit)"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:136
msgid ""
"The audits you have been given access to, in read only: controls, progress, "
"submitted evidence and findings."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:141
msgid ""
"Open an audit, then download the submitted documents. Every download is "
"recorded. Your access ends on the date set by the organisation."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:149
msgid ""
"The register of all the contracts with ICT third-party service providers "
"that DORA requires: contracts, providers and their subcontractors, functions "
"supported and their criticality, data locations, substitutability and exit "
"plans. It is built from GLPI contracts, suppliers and business processes."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:156
msgid ""
"Fill in the financial entity below, then add each ICT contract from its "
"\"DORA register\" tab and complete the missing fields listed here. When "
"nothing is missing, download the templates and give them to your reporting "
"tool."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:161
msgid "DORA, article 28(3); Implementing Regulation (EU) 2024/2956"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:165
msgid ""
"Assessment by framework: for each enabled framework, how many of its "
"controls are implemented, how many are proven by valid evidence, and the "
"resulting score."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:170
msgid ""
"Open the gaps of a framework, then update each control or attach the missing "
"evidence; an expired document no longer counts. Present the scores at the "
"management review."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:174
msgid "ISO 27001, 9.1 and 9.3; mapping of each framework to Annex A"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:178
msgid ""
"Automated technical checks: checks computed from GLPI data (antivirus, disk "
"encryption, inventory, change validation, accounts), with a score per "
"framework."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:183
msgid ""
"Review the gaps of each check and create the remediation ticket; once the "
"items are fixed, the score goes up. Present the scores at the management "
"review."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:187
msgid "ISO 27001, 9.1; NIS2, article 21; GDPR, article 32"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:191
msgid ""
"Crisis exercises: simulate an incident (ransomware, data leak, outage) to "
"check that the team knows how to react and that the continuity plan works."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:196
msgid ""
"Start a scenario: a fictitious \"EXERCISE\" incident is created with one "
"task per step. In the crisis room, tick each step as soon as it is done; at "
"the end, the report measures reaction times and serves as audit evidence. At "
"least one exercise per year."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:201
msgid "ISO 27001, Annex A 5.29 and 5.30"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:205
msgid ""
"The information security risk register: each risk is assessed (likelihood × "
"impact), linked to the assets it threatens and to the controls that reduce "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:210
msgid ""
"Identify risks, assess them, decide on a treatment (reduce, accept, "
"transfer, avoid) and set a review date. The owner is notified when it is due."
