msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, control A.5.32"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:401
msgid ""
"The context of the organization: the internal and external issues that "
"affect information security, and the interested parties with their "
"expectations and what the ISMS retains."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:406
msgid ""
"List the issues and the interested parties, decide for each one whether the "
"ISMS retains it, link the related risks, obligations and controls, answer "
"the climate change question, and review each item at least once a year. Use "
"the export of the list for the auditor."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:411
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, clauses 4.1 and 4.2"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:416
msgid ""
"Shows whether each main IT operations activity (backup, restore, monitoring, "
"updates...) has a documented procedure that is approved and reviewed on "
"time, with its version, its owner and who has acknowledged it."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:422
msgid ""
"For each domain without an up-to-date procedure, add one or update it: "
"attach the document, have it approved, set its next review date, then launch "
"the reading acknowledgement for the groups or profiles that carry it out. "
"Archive the register on control A.5.37 before an audit."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:428
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, control A.5.37"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:433
msgid ""
"Who to contact outside the organization when something happens: authorities "
"(data protection authority, national CSIRT, police), regulators, insurers "
"and special interest groups, with their details, when to contact them, the "
"time limit and who is allowed to call them."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:439
msgid ""
"Record each official contact, tick the events for which it must be informed, "
"verify the details at least once a year, and keep a printed copy of the "
"register (PDF) for use during a crisis."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:444
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, controls A.5.5 and A.5.6"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:448
msgid ""
"Who performs, approves, is consulted on or is informed of each activity of "
"the ISMS, with the GLPI users and groups. Conflicts of duties and missing "
"approvers are reported here."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:453
msgid ""
"For each activity, add who performs it and a single approver, mark the "
"sensitive activities, fix the alerts, then archive the matrix as evidence "
"before the audit."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:457
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, clause 5.3 and control A.5.3"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:462
msgid ""
"The competences each ISMS function needs (CISO, DPO, administrator...), who "
"holds each function, what each person has acquired through passed trainings "
"or declared evidence, and the gaps."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:467
msgid ""
"Add the functions and their required competences with the expected level, "
"say who holds them, link the trainings that give each competence, declare "
"the certificates and diplomas, plan the proposed actions, then archive the "
"file as evidence before the audit."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:472 src/PageHelp.php:484 src/PageHelp.php:497
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, clause 7.2"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:476
msgid ""
"The catalogue of the information security competences of the organization, "
"and the trainings that give each one once passed."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:481
msgid ""
"Describe each competence and link the trainings that give it, with the level "
"reached."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:488
msgid ""
"The competences acquired outside the trainings of the plugin, each one with "
"its evidence: certificate, diploma, annual review or proven experience."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:493
msgid ""
"Record the reference of the evidence, its date and its end of validity, and "
"attach the file in the Documents tab."
msgstr ""

