msgid "ISO 27001, 9.2.2; ISO 19011, 5"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:543
msgid ""
"Nonconformities and observations, with their corrective and preventive "
"actions (CAPA)."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:547
msgid ""
"Analyse the cause, describe the corrective action, assign an owner and a due "
"date, then check its effectiveness before closing."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:551
msgid "ISO 27001, 10.2"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:555
msgid ""
"Security training and awareness sessions, with their participants and "
"results."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:559
msgid ""
"Record each session, its participants and its renewal date; a reminder is "
"sent when it is due."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:562
msgid "ISO 27001, 7.2 and 7.3"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:566
msgid ""
"Management reviews: the periodic review of the information security "
"management system by top management."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:571
msgid ""
"At least once a year, prepare the review (indicators, audits, incidents, "
"risks), record the decisions and the resulting actions."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:575
msgid "ISO 27001, 9.3"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:578
msgid "Security objectives and their indicators measured over time."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:580
msgid ""
"Define measurable objectives, enter the measurements each period and track "
"progress towards the target."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:584
msgid "ISO 27001, 6.2 and 9.1"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:588
msgid ""
"Access rights review campaigns: each manager confirms or removes the rights "
"of their team."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:592
msgid ""
"Start a campaign; managers decide line by line. Removing a right opens a "
"ticket, it is never applied automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:596
msgid "ISO 27001, Annex A 5.18"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:600
msgid ""
"Accounts to check: inactive accounts, accounts missing from the directory, "
"duplicates or never used."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:605
msgid ""
"Review the list and open a ticket for each account to disable; nothing is "
"disabled automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:612
msgid ""
"Security compliance of each person: screening, confidentiality agreement, "
"mandatory trainings, IT charter, security policies read, access review and "
"account hygiene."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:617
msgid ""
"Follow up the gaps with the person and their manager; nothing is changed "
"automatically. The deadline for newcomers and the weight of each component "
"are set in the plugin configuration."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:622
msgid "ISO 27001, Annex A 6.1, 6.2, 6.3, 6.5, 6.6 and 5.18"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:626
msgid ""
"Periodic reviews (backups, logs, rights, continuity plan...) scheduled as "
"recurring tickets."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:630
msgid ""
"Enable the useful reviews and their frequency; a ticket is created at each "
"due date for the person in charge."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:637
msgid ""
"The matrix of authorised network flows: who talks to whom, on which port, "
"and why."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:641
msgid ""
"Describe each flow with its justification and owner, or import your firewall "
"export, then review the matrix regularly."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:645
msgid "ISO 27001, Annex A 8.20 to 8.22"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:649
msgid ""
"Work email addresses found in known data breaches (Have I Been Pwned), "
"checked every day."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:653
msgid ""
"For each new exposure, have the password changed (and enable multi-factor "
"authentication) if passwords were exposed, then mark it as handled."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:657
msgid "ISO 27001, Annex A 5.7 and 5.17"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:661
msgid ""
"The compliance calendar: all due dates (reviews, audits, renewals, "
"obligations) in one place, also visible in the GLPI planning."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:666
msgid ""
"Check it to anticipate due dates; subscribe your calendar with the iCal link."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:672
msgid ""
"One-off compliance events to add to the calendar (regulator inspection, "
"crisis exercise, contractual deadline...)."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:677
msgid ""
"Add the event with its date and owner; it appears in the compliance calendar."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:683
msgid ""
"The library of security policies, versioned, with their approval and review "
"date."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:687
msgid ""
"Upload each policy, have it approved, distribute it and review it when due."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:690
msgid "ISO 27001, 5.2; Annex A 5.1"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:694
msgid "Dated evidence (reports, attestations, certificates) and its validity."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:698
msgid ""
"State how long each piece of evidence is valid; a renewal ticket is opened "
"when it expires."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:704
msgid ""
"The effectiveness tests of the Annex A controls: a control in place is "
"checked to really work, with its method, result and evidence."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:709
msgid ""
"Set a test plan on each control, record each test from the control's "
"\"Effectiveness tests\" tab and carry out the tests that are due first. An "
"ineffective control opens a non-conformity."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:714
msgid "ISO 27001, 9.1; ISO 27002, 5.35 and 5.36"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:718
msgid ""
"The audit log of the security incidents: who consulted or changed what, "
"when, with which profile and from which address, including impersonations."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:723
msgid ""
"Filter the entries, export them for an audit or a court, and check the "
"integrity regularly: each entry is sealed with the previous one."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:730
msgid ""
"Import of a CSV export of the alerts from an EDR or XDR console: each alert "
"becomes an incident with its indicators, MITRE ATT&CK techniques, hosts and "
"accounts."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:735
msgid ""
"Check the columns proposed, choose how to group the alerts, then import. An "
"alert already imported is ignored; the original lines are kept unchanged on "
"the incident."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:742
msgid ""
"EBIOS Risk Manager studies: the risk assessment method of ANSSI, the French "
"national cybersecurity agency, published under an open licence."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:747
msgid ""
"Create one study per scope, then work through its workshops in order: "
"business values and feared events, risk sources, stakeholders and strategic "
"scenarios, operational scenarios, then their treatment, which feeds the risk "
"register."
msgstr ""

