msgid ""
"Custom frameworks: follow a framework that is not built in (group "
"requirements, sector or contractual framework, customer security plan) by "
"importing it from a spreadsheet."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:773
msgid ""
"Download the template, fill in one line per requirement with the Annex A "
"controls that meet it, import it, then enable the framework. A new version "
"of the file updates it without losing the statuses already entered."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:781
msgid ""
"Coverage rules: which assets must have which document (for example, every "
"server must have its operations sheet)."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:786
msgid ""
"Create one rule per requirement; the result lists the covered assets and "
"those to complete."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:792
msgid ""
"Security exemptions: accepted exceptions to a policy or a control, limited "
"in time and compensated."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:797
msgid ""
"Justify each exemption, describe the compensating measures, have it approved "
"and set its end date; it is reassessed when due."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:801
msgid "ISO 27001, 6.1.3; Annex A 5.36"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:805
msgid ""
"Business processes: who owns them, how critical they are, how long they can "
"be interrupted and which GLPI items they depend on."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:810
msgid ""
"For each process, rate the impact of an interruption over time (business "
"impact analysis), set its MTPD, RTO and RPO, and link the applications, "
"servers and suppliers it needs; items slower than the process are reported. "
"Export the result for your continuity plan."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:815
msgid "ISO 22301, 8.2.2; ISO 27001, Annex A 5.29 and 5.30"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:819
msgid ""
"Single points of failure: critical items that depend on a single source, "
"according to GLPI's impact analysis."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:824
msgid ""
"Create the matching risk or add redundancy; export the list for your "
"business continuity plan."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:827
msgid "ISO 27001, Annex A 5.29, 5.30 and 8.14"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:830
msgid "The domino effect: how one incident or risk can lead to others."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:832
msgid ""
"Link items from the \"Domino effect\" tab of a risk or an incident; this "
"page shows the whole picture."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:839
msgid ""
"Security incidents: qualification, affected assets, CVEs, costs, regulatory "
"notifications (data protection authority, NIS2)."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:844
msgid ""
"Declare the incident, qualify it, follow up the actions and meet the "
"notification deadlines shown on the record."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:848
msgid "ISO 27001, Annex A 5.24 to 5.28"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:852
msgid ""
"Known vulnerabilities (CVEs) of the software installed on your fleet, with "
"their real-world exploitation (KEV, EPSS) and CERT-FR advisories."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:857
msgid ""
"Handle exploited and priority vulnerabilities first; open one update ticket "
"per software."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:860 src/PageHelp.php:884
msgid "ISO 27001, Annex A 8.8"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:864
msgid ""
"Fleet software to match with a CPE reference so that its vulnerabilities are "
"tracked."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:868
msgid ""
"Start with the most exposed (browsers, remote access, VPN): search for the "
"CPE, confirm it, or ignore software with no stakes."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:875
msgid ""
"The machines most exposed to the known vulnerabilities of their watched "
"software, to know where to start updating."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:880
msgid ""
"Handle the machines at the top of the list first; the \"Vulnerabilities\" "
"tab of each one details the CVEs and the update ticket."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:888
msgid ""
"The correlation catalogue: reference products, their CPEs and the names "
"under which they appear in the inventory."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:893
msgid ""
"It is filled from \"Software to watch\"; correct an alias or a CPE here if "
"needed."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:899
msgid ""
"Mappings between Annex A and other frameworks, to reuse your work across "
"several standards."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:902
msgid "Check the mappings before an audit against another framework."
msgstr ""

